messages.reasoning_content:
Good.

`pixelsPerUnit` on image setter maybe requires? Let's inspect. It sets and refreshMesh. Fine.

Now fake app design details:
```
import { EventHandler } from '../../../../src/core/event-handler.js';
import { NullGraphicsDevice } from '../../../../src/platform/graphics/null/null-graphics-device.js';
```
Need check export path. Null graphics device public? It exists. Does importing NullGraphicsDevice work standalone? It extends GraphicsDevice etc; likely.

Could use `createGraphicsDevice` with null? Not needed.

Create fake:
```
function createApp() {
 const app = new EventHandler();
 app.graphicsDevice = new NullGraphicsDevice();
 app.scene = new EventHandler();
 app.scene.layers = new EventHandler();
 app.scene.layers.getLayerById = () => ({ addMeshInstances(){}, removeMeshInstances(){} });
 app.i18n = new EventHandler();
 app.i18n.locale = 'en';
 app.i18n.getText = (key) => key;
 app.assets = new EventHandler();
 app.assets.get = () => null;
 app.elementInput = null;
 app.batcher = null;
 app.systems = {};
 return app;
}
```
But ElementComponentSystem `super(app)` doesn't register itself in app.systems. Text `_updateText` uses `system.app.systems.element.getRtlReorder()` only if rtlReorder true. If testing rtlReorder behavior, need app.systems.element = system. Could set after constructing system: `app.systems.element = system`.

`app.once` from EventHandler yes. ElementComponent `_dirtifyMask` maybe app.once. Not needed.

Also `app.graphicsDevice` destruction after each test. NullGraphicsDevice.destroy() maybe fine. Could do afterAll or per test to avoid leaks. Each system creates texture; we can destroy system in afterEach and maybe device.destroy(). But after system.destroy(), test file may still use device? We'll set up per test.

Could avoid creating NullGraphicsDevice per test by a single device shared, but then system.destroy() default texture destroy fine. Yet tests independent. Creating device per test is maybe slow but okay (~dozens tests). However if each test creates system and device, cleanup. Use beforeEach? Each test likely gets fresh app/system. Simpler.

But creating StandardMaterial is cheap. NullGraphicsDevice maybe moderate.

Alternative fake graphicsDevice object could satisfy Texture and Image mesh creation. But real device safer and deterministic.

Let's prototype a basic test file with setup and run one test to catch issues.

